{"kind":"request","text":"J4 implementation boundary, prepared while 121a gate-2 runs. This requests a design disposition, not permission to deploy or a change to the current order.\n\nI read J4 0c3091fa, plan029, the MVP plan, plan032 and current Main4c333 source. The scratch source map is /private/tmp/artroom-j4-workspace-source-preparation-20261029/SOURCE-MAP.md (10,551 bytes, SHA256 01f65b17a45d5f45b62f62401783b6d0c50f82d38c33c568700132410a50b2fc). No provider, credential, deployment or implementation action ran.\n\nThree concrete decisions are needed for the later J4 dispatch:\n\n1. Original J4 depends on MVP S0's hold-staging finding, but the effective order puts J4 before S0/S1. No actual S0 finding was found in the inspected order or tracked notes. Identify that existing finding or explicitly dispose of this prerequisite; do not infer a deployed success or failure from source.\n\n2. Current hold@1 code derives fork/head requests but OPERATION_RULES (packages/derive/src/capability/hold.ts:792-899) has no fork/head outcome rule. Ending a hold derives token revocations; fork deletion requires explicit safe retirement rather than the automatic end/sweeper lifecycle described by plan029. Adopt the smallest rule/version extension needed for J4's required distinct forks, revocation and chosen-fork publication, preserving historical recorded meaning. State whether automatic deletion/sweeping remains later work. This is a kernel filing/design boundary, not only a provider transport switch.\n\n3. Choose the first provider scope. Artifacts has retained real fork/read/revoke/delete measurements (notes/implementation/2026-10-13-fork-cost-measurement.md); info exposes no status field. Existing host selection and credential delivery admit native Register/Destination only, so J4 also needs authenticated lane lineage, hold-bound private custody and selected-fork publication. Propose an Artifacts-first bounded adapter with GitHub separately assigned unless the acceptance requires both now. Current GitHubProvider already supports active token revocation, so the older plan's expiry-only statement cannot govern the new implementation.\n\nThe existing J4 acceptance remains concrete: two agents push to their own hold forks, the old token actually fails at the provider after its hold ends, and the chosen fork publishes. Deployment authorization already exists. Keep current order 121a → proof reuse7c0 → J4; the current source and gate are independent of this disposition.","body":{"conditions":"Resolve J4's missing S0 prerequisite and adopt the smallest provider/rule-version scope for its existing acceptance, before implementation. Current 121a and the ordered proof-reuse task continue independently.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}